@startuml wide-screen-splits
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif

participant "User / Settings Modal" as UI
participant "SettingsWindowController" as Settings
participant "ScreenManager" as ScreenMgr
participant "CascadeEngine" as Engine
participant "macOS Displays\n(Quartz / Cocoa)" as Displays

== Screen Split Configuration ==
UI -> Settings : Select Display ("C49RG9x 49\" Ultrawide")\nSelect Columns: [1 | 2 | 3 | 4] (e.g. 3)
Settings -> ScreenMgr : saveScreenSplit:3 forScreenName:@"C49RG9x"
ScreenMgr -> ScreenMgr : Persist to NSUserDefaults\n(key: "screenSplit_name_C49RG9x" = 3)
Settings -> Settings : Synchronize UI state

== Cascade Execution on Ultrawide Screen ==
UI -> Engine : Trigger Cascade (Menu, Shortcut ⌥⌘C, or CLI)
Engine -> ScreenMgr : availableScreens
ScreenMgr -> Displays : Query NSScreen / CGDirectDisplayID
Displays --> ScreenMgr : [0] C49RG9x (5120x1440)\n[1] Retina (1800x1169)

Engine -> ScreenMgr : expandScreensWithSplits(screens)
note over ScreenMgr
  For each display:
  - Query screenSplitForScreen:
  - C49RG9x -> 3 Columns
  - Slices visible frame (5120x1410):
    * Col 0: [X: 0, W: 1706]
    * Col 1: [X: 1706, W: 1706]
    * Col 2: [X: 3412, W: 1708]
  - Retina -> 1 Column [X: 2646, W: 1800]
end note
ScreenMgr --> Engine : 4 Virtual CascadeScreens

== Window Partitioning & Auto-Rebalancing ==
Engine -> ScreenMgr : partitionWindows:allWindows intoScreens:expandedScreens
note over ScreenMgr
  1. Spatial Attribution:
     Assign window to column by maximum area overlap.
  2. Empty Column Protection:
     If any column is empty and total windows >= columns,
     automatically balance windows evenly across columns!
end note
ScreenMgr --> Engine : Partition Dictionary: {Col0: [W1, W2], Col1: [W3, W4], Col2: [W5, W6]}

== Invariant-Preserving Layout Calculation ==
loop For each virtual column screen
  Engine -> Engine : calculateLayoutForWindows:delta:onUsableFrame:
  note over Engine
    Within Column Bounds:
    - Width: 73%..98% of Column Width
    - Height: Usable Screen Height
    - Step Offset (Delta: 40px)
    - Click Tabs Guaranteed Disjoint!
  end note
  Engine -> Displays : Apply Window Frames via Accessibility API
end

@enduml
